    public Day day;
```
- `date` - stores the date as a String (e.g., "2025-12-05")
- `day` - stores a `Day` object which contains all the weather details (temp, condition, rain, etc.)

**Why separate them?**
- `date` is just text, simple to store
- `day` is complex (has temperature, condition, humidity, etc.), so we put it in its own `Day` class

